+++
title = "Section Hike of the John Muir Trail"
date = "2023-09-01"
tags = ["trip-report"]
draft = true
+++

In August we hiked the first stretch of the John Muir Trail southbound. We went out of Yosemite Valley, up Half Dome, through Tuolumne Meadows and Lyell Canyon, over Donohue Pass, past the Thousand Island and Garnet Lake country, and down to Red's Meadow.

The trail was beautiful. We had one (kinda scary) bear encounter and one bout of altitude sickness. The bear encounter was in Tuolumne. We had just crested a small hill and came right up on a big black bear. It was about 10 feet in front of us --- we spooked it --- so that lead to an uncomfortable 15 minute standoff. _Backup, turn, backup some more, turn, "HEY BEAR"..._ It followed us for a bit and then finally got bored and went up the other side of the valley.

The mileage to Red's Meadow is roughly 57-60 miles from Happy Isles depending on the source and exact route. With Half Dome and the Mammoth exit added in, the trip was about 75 miles over five days. We had a great time!

